 ## Overview
-Visibility Field Computation calculates the specific contribution of each voxel to the final 2D image, accounting for its own opacity and the occlusion caused by preceding voxels along the viewing ray [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from standard ray casting by explicitly storing these per-voxel visibility weights in a data structure, enabling analysis of which parts of the volume contribute most to the image and how tissues occlude one another [S2, unofficial].
