 ## Background
-The concept of voxel visibility as a contribution metric originates from early volume rendering research, specifically Levoy (1988) [S1, unofficial]. The term "Visibility Field" and its use in saliency analysis were formalized by Luo and Dingliana (2015) [S2, unofficial]. The method is often implemented using CUDA or OpenGL shaders for performance [S1, S2, unofficial].
